-- Q2937: Financial Statement Analysis [medium/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The divergence signals premature revenue recognition under ASC 606, inflating the top line while net income corrects for the overstatement","The divergence is expected because revenue growth always outpaces net income growth in expanding companies due to economies of scale","The divergence most likely indicates costs are growing faster than revenue, compressing margins through rising input costs, pricing pressure, or a product mix shift","The divergence indicates share repurchases reduced net income while leaving revenue unchanged"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 205-10-45, when revenue grows 38% (index 138) while net income declines 2% (index 98), costs are consuming more than all incremental revenue — indicating margin compression from rising COGS, expanding SG&A, or a shift toward lower-margin products.
Wrong (A): Premature revenue recognition would inflate both revenue and net income simultaneously, not create a divergence between them.
Wrong (B): Economies of scale should improve margins, causing net income to grow faster than revenue — the opposite of the observed pattern.
Wrong (D): Share repurchases reduce equity and may affect EPS, but they do not reduce net income or explain the divergence.$EXPL$
